# encode_surrogate_reject.tkr — the SM-STRU32 codec fixture. `main.tks` feeds
# `teko::text::encode_u32_utf8` a single codepoint U+D800 (a UTF-16 surrogate, not a scalar
# value) and exits 0 only if the call returns `error` (never a fabricated byte sequence).

Feature: encode_surrogate_reject — encode_u32_utf8 rejects a surrogate codepoint

  Scenario: surrogate_codepoint_u_d800_is_rejected
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
